Executive Summary
The Marbleshore presentation will outline the end-to-end insurance process and data flows for a planned system integration project. It will cover both the Underwriting/Policy Issuance workflow and the Premium & Claims Bordereaux workflow, identify key roles, systems, and data exchanges, and detail the integration design (e.g. the UWC→ASCO and SRM→EDW feeds). The audience is assumed to be Marbleshore underwriting managers, IT architects, and project stakeholders. We assume no existing corporate PowerPoint template, so a clean, professional theme will be used with Marbleshore corporate-style colors (blue/grays)[1]. The deck will have 10 slides (plus title), ~45–60 minutes total. Each slide is timed ~4–6 minutes (more for complex diagrams). Key milestones and data integration details will be highlighted.
Purpose, Audience & Assumptions
•	Purpose: To present Marbleshore’s new integrated underwriting/bordereaux solution – its processes, system architecture, timeline, and next steps – in a concise executive-level slide deck.
•	Audience: Underwriting/Actuarial managers, IT/Data architects, Project sponsors, and selected partners (brokers/coverholders). The content is technical but non-IT-savvy stakeholders should be accommodated (brief speaker notes explain jargon).
•	Assumptions: The audience is familiar with basic insurance terms but not the specific Marbleshore systems. We assume Marbleshore brand guidelines allow a blue/gray theme, and that we should not include any Safelite-specific details beyond slide structure. Unspecified items (e.g. exact launch date) will be noted as “TBD” or based on earliest estimates.
Slide Count & Timing
•	Total Slides: 10 (including title and concluding slides). This matches the example Safelite deck.
•	Timing: ~4–6 minutes per slide, total ~45–60 min talk. The timeline slide and architecture slides may take slightly longer (6–7 min), simpler bullet slides can be ~3–4 min. Pace should allow Q&A prompts.
