Slide 6: Bordereaux (Premium & Claims) Process
•	Title: “Premium & Claims Bordereaux Process”
•	Content: Four phases (as per Marbleshore_high_level_flow):
•	1. Receipt & Triage: Coverholder/TPA uploads monthly bordereaux (Excel/CSV) via email/SFTP/portal. PCS team logs file in Premium-Claims Services (PC-S) platform.
•	2. Processing & Validation: Processor uploads bordereau into PC-S; automatic column mapping and data validation runs. Exceptions (invalid/missing data) are flagged and resolved (via email to coverholder).
•	3. Reconciliation & Booking: Validated premium totals are reconciled with cash received. PCS team and Finance allocate payments in the accounting system (Exact). Validated claims are reviewed (with IMR for reference) and payment instructions are prepared.
•	4. Reporting & Closure: Finalized bordereau data is archived. PCS generates reports (by Excel/PDF) for underwriters, finance, and management.
•	Visual: (Optional) A simplified flow diagram or list with arrows between icons labeled “Receive → Validate → Reconcile → Report”.
•	Speaker Notes: Stress that processing is largely automated in PC-S, with human review of exceptions. Mention key systems (PC-S, Exact, IMR) at each stage.
