Slide 8: Exception Handling & Reconciliation
•	Title: “Exception Handling & Data Reconciliation”
•	Content: Bulleted points on controls and exception processes:
•	Automated Validations: All data feeds (bordereaux, SRM loads) run row-level checks (e.g. totals, policy existence). Pre-Validation jobs verify record counts and send alerts on mismatch.
•	Exception Alerts: If record counts or data validations fail, an automated email alert is sent to the Support/Data team[2]. A work order is opened to investigate (e.g. contact coverholder for corrected bordereau).
•	Reconciliation Steps: Premium totals are reconciled with the finance ledger (Exact). Discrepancies trigger follow-up (e.g. remittance advice errors).
•	Exception Resolution: Problem cases are tracked in PCS/UWC; once corrected data is reprocessed, confirmations are sent to stakeholders.
•	Visual: Possibly a small flowchart (e.g. “Job Scheduler → Pre-Validation → (OK vs ERROR) → Load Process → Notification” – no actual image needed).
•	Speaker Notes: Emphasize that robust controls are in place: every data feed has a “control file” with row counts/hash totals. Any mismatch halts the load and notifies support. This avoids “undetected data loss.”
