Slide Design & Style Guidelines
•	Theme: Use a professional, modern theme (e.g. a blue/gray palette). Each slide should use the same master (matching Marbleshore colors). Titles in bold (e.g. Calibri Bold 32pt), body text in Calibri 20–24pt for readability.
•	Fonts: Sans-serif (Calibri or Arial) for clarity. Consistent size/hierarchy: Title > Heading > Body. Avoid small text (<18pt).
•	Colors: High-contrast text (dark on light). Marbleshore brand colors (if known) or “blue accents” for headers. Use color sparingly – e.g. one accent color per chart or diagram.
•	Charts & Graphics: Use simple vector diagrams (Mermaid-style charts, tables) where possible. Icons or minimal stock photos can illustrate points (e.g. user icon for roles, process flow arrows).
•	Accessibility: Ensure 4.5:1 contrast (e.g. dark blue on white). All images/diagrams have alt text. Bullet points kept short (no paragraphs).
•	Layout: Left-align text; use whitespace. Keep 5–6 bullet points per slide max. Include slide numbers. Footer can have confidential tag, date, and logo if desired.
