Slide 8: Exception Handling & Reconciliation
- Validation Checks: Each data transfer (bordereaux feeds, SRM extracts) is pre-validated. Automated jobs compare expected vs actual row counts[2].
- Failure Alerts: If counts mismatch or data errors occur, an alert email is sent immediately to the Data/Support team with details.
- Resolve Exceptions: Processor investigates: e.g. if a bordereau file failed validation, they contact the coverholder for corrections. Corrections are re-uploaded and re-processed.
- Reconciliation Controls: Premium bordereaux are reconciled daily against banking ledgers. Discrepancies trigger follow-up (e.g. misapplied payments).
- Audit Trail: All exceptions and resolutions are logged in PC-S/UWC (audit history). Reports highlight outstanding issues weekly.
Slide 9: Support Model & Escalation Path
- Support Teams:
- L1 (Operations Team): Monitors daily jobs (PCS, ETL). First responders to alerts. Maintains runbooks.
- L2 (Data/IT Team): Investigates data issues or job failures. Develops fixes for ETL or mapping errors.
- L3 (Dev/Engineering): Handles code updates to UWC/PCS/ASCO and complex bug fixes.
- Escalation: Unresolved incidents are escalated from L1 → L2 → L3. Critical issues notify project leads and management.
- Service Levels:
- Critical (jobs down): 15-min response, 2-hour fix (hotfix or rollback).
- High: 1-hour response, 4-hour resolution.
- Normal: Next-business-day response.
- Hypercare Period: Full-time support for 4 weeks post-launch, then transition to steady-state support.
- Monitoring: Key metrics (load success, exception rates) are tracked on a dashboard for early warning.
Slide 10: Non-Functional Requirements & Standards
- Security: All data feeds use SFTP + PGP encryption (AES-256). Files named per spec: UWC_ASCO_YYYYMMDD.txt.gpg.
- Format: Pipe-delimited UTF-8 text with header row. Separate control file (.ctl) with row count and hash totals is sent with each load.
- Frequency/Timing: Daily after 2:00 AM UTC. Data aligns with end-of-day processing in PCS/UWC.
- Error Handling: Failed transfers trigger automated alerts (email/IM). Manual rerun allowed after issue is fixed; rerun results reconciled by team.
- Performance: ETL jobs should complete within 4 hours; system can process ~1M records/day. Overnight loads minimize business impact.
- Compliance: Adheres to corporate data standards (GDPR compliance on PII encryption, audit logs enabled).
- Accessibility: Reports use clear fonts and color for charts. Slide deck follows AA contrast guidelines.
